I recommend putting the files in the default templates search path, which is a
subdirectory of ~/texmf/tex/latex.  It can be any named subdirectory.  For
example, you can use git to clone it:

    git clone https://github.com/markwkm/postgres-beamer-template.git ~/texmf/tex/latex/postgres

If you are not sure where your personal texmf tree is, this prints it:

    kpsewhich -var-value=TEXMFHOME

To use the template, just add:

\usetheme{postgres}

...

% the plain option omits the footer from the title page
\frame[plain]{\titlepage}


If you want 16:9 instead of the default 4:3 aspect ratio:

\documentclass[aspectratio=169]{beamer}
